        "abstract": "This paper presents the relationship of dielectric properties to determine and predict the papaya fruit quality. The duration for this sampling is seven days from unripe to full-ripe condition. Two techniques are used which is a non-destructive and destructive technique. For the non-destructive method, capacitive sensing was used to find papaya output voltage and capacitance value. Moisture content and TSS content are used for the destructive technique to predict the correlation with the nondestructive technique. Four different frequencies have been used to get the various output voltage and different papaya capacitance. Four different frequency is varied from 250k to 1.5M Hz. From the result, 1.5M Hz is the best and suitable for papaya fruit based on the correlation between capacitance, moisture content and TSS measurement. The value obtained of R<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">2</sup> is 0.9434 and 0.9177, respectively using linear regression. Different output voltage also shows a good correlation with TSS content and moisture content. Therefore, papaya fruit quality can be predicted by using capacitive sensing technique.",
